  "notes": "{黙|だま}る means to become silent or stop talking, often implying a deliberate choice to remain quiet.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{黙|だま}っている indicates the state of being silent or keeping quiet.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {黙|だま}ったまま: remaining silent, without speaking\n- {黙|だま}って + verb: silently doing something\n- {黙|だま}っていてください: please be quiet\n- {黙|だま}りこむ: to fall into silence (compound verb)\n\nRELATED EXPRESSIONS:\n- {黙|だま}れ: Shut up! (imperative, rude)\n- {沈黙|ちんもく}: silence (noun, formal)\n\nNOTE:\n{黙|だま}って often implies doing something without asking permission or informing others: {黙|だま}って{出|で}かける (to leave without saying anything).",
